  "rationale": "The plant G models the robot's possible motion and perception event sequences in a grid-world, including all controllable and uncontrollable events. The specification E enforces safe exploration, immediate escape from blue danger, and obstacle-aware movement, only allowing move_backward as a front-obstacle recovery, and requiring escape_blue after blue_detected. The design prioritizes forward exploration, uses conservative recovery only when needed, and ensures all controllable actions are reachable somewhere in the automaton.",
  "strategy": [
    "Use helper states for action commits and recovery, ensuring only one controllable action per state and deterministic transitions.",
    "Prioritize move_forward in clear states, use rotate_clockwise for left obstacles, rotate_counterclockwise for right obstacles, and reserve full_rotate for last-resort recovery after repeated blockages. Escape from blue area is immediate and mandatory."
